{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" owns a world and a set of schedules, each named by a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". You add"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"systems to the schedules by label, then call "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" once a frame with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time that passed. The simulation decides which schedules run:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/startup"},{"type":"text","text":" runs once, before the first frame."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs once for every fixed timestep of time that has passed, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics and other rate-sensitive rules advance by the same amount each run, however uneven the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frames are."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/update","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs once a frame."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and systems:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double }","struct FixedSteps: Resource { var count = 0 }","enum GameState: States { case menu, playing, paused }","","\/\/\/ Moves each entity by its velocity over one fixed timestep.","@System","struct Physics {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>, _ fixedTime: ResourceReader<FixedTime>) {","        let seconds = fixedTime.value.timestep \/ .seconds(1)","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx * seconds","        }","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Counts the runs of the schedule it is in.","@System","struct CountSteps {","    func run(_ steps: ResourceWriter<FixedSteps>) {","        steps.value.count += 1","    }","}","","\/\/\/ Spawns a ball at the origin.","@System","struct SpawnBall {","    func run(commands: inout Commands) {","        commands.spawn(Position(x: 0), Velocity(dx: 64))","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example runs "},{"code":"Physics","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on a fixed timestep of 1\/64 second, the default. A frame"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of 50 milliseconds covers three whole timesteps, so the ball moves three times:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0), Velocity(dx: 64))","","var simulation = Simulation(world)","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Physics() }","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","","print(simulation.world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0)\""]},{"anchor":"States","type":"heading","text":"States","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A state type is a type, usually an enumeration, that conforms to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States"},{"type":"text","text":": the screens of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game, or the phases of a simulation. Add one to a simulation with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/add(state:)"},{"type":"text","text":". The simulation keeps the current state in the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"resource; to change it, a system sets "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState"},{"type":"text","text":", and the change applies at the start of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next frame. Entering, leaving and moving between states run schedules of their own,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onEnter(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onExit(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onTransition(from:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" makes a run condition that holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only in one state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example spawns a ball on entering the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"playing"},{"type":"text","text":" state and moves it only while the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game is in that state:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var simulation = Simulation()","simulation.add(state: GameState.menu)","simulation.add(to: .onEnter(GameState.playing)) { SpawnBall() }","simulation.add(to: .fixedUpdate) { Physics().runIf(inState(GameState.playing)) }","","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","print(simulation.world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"0\"","","simulation.world.resources[NextState<GameState>.self].set(.playing)","simulation.update(elapsed: .milliseconds(50))","print(simulation.world.resources[CurrentState<GameState>.self].state)","\/\/ Prints \"playing\"","for (_, position) in simulation.world.query(Position.self) {","    print(position)  \/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 3.0)\"","}"]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with states that switch systems on and off."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Simulations","anchor":"Simulations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NonPositiveDuration"]},{"title":"Time","anchor":"Time","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Time","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/FixedTime"]},{"title":"States","anchor":"States","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"SimulationModule","modules":[{"name":"SimulationModule"}],"symbolKind":"module","title":"SimulationModule","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/simulationmodule"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"references":{"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation/add(state:)":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation\/add(state:)","abstract":[{"text":"Adds a state type to the simulation, starting in the given state.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"add","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"state"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/add(state:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"add(state:)"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/onTransition(from:to:)":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/ontransition(from:to:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the label of the schedule that runs when a simulation changes from one given state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to another."}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"onTransition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onTransition(from:to:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"onTransition(from:to:)"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleLabel"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduleLabel"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The name of a schedule in a simulation."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel","title":"ScheduleLabel"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/inState(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Returns a run condition that holds when a world’s current state is the given state.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"inState"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> (","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/inState(_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"inState(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/instate(_:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation/update(elapsed:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation\/update(elapsed:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"update"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"elapsed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Advances the simulation by one frame.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation\/update(elapsed:)","title":"update(elapsed:)"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule":{"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule","kind":"symbol","title":"SimulationModule","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with states that switch systems on and off.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/NextState":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/nextstate","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NextState"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NextState"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource holding the state a simulation enters at the start of its next frame."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NextState","title":"NextState"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/CurrentState":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/currentstate","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CurrentState","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CurrentState","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource holding the state a simulation is in."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/CurrentState","title":"CurrentState"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation":{"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation","title":"Simulation","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Simulation","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A world and its schedules by label, advanced one frame at a time.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Simulation","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/States":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/states","abstract":[{"text":"A type whose values are the states a simulation can be in.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"States","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"States","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/States","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"States"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/update":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The label of the schedule that runs once a frame."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"update"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/update","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"update","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/update","role":"symbol"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/FixedTime":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/fixedtime","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FixedTime"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FixedTime"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A resource holding the fixed timestep of a simulation.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/FixedTime","title":"FixedTime"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/fixedUpdate":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/fixedupdate","abstract":[{"text":"The label of the schedule that runs once for each fixed timestep of elapsed time.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fixedUpdate"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/fixedUpdate","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"fixedUpdate"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/onExit(_:)":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/onexit(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Returns the label of the schedule that runs when a simulation leaves the given state.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"onExit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"S","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleLabel","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onExit(_:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"onExit(_:)"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Time":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/time","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Time","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Time","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A resource holding the time a simulation has advanced.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Time","title":"Time"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/startup":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/startup","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"startup","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScheduleLabel"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The label of the schedule that runs once, before the first frame.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/startup","title":"startup"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/NonPositiveDuration":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An error that indicates a simulation’s fixed timestep or maximum frame time is zero or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"negative."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NonPositiveDuration"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/NonPositiveDuration","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NonPositiveDuration"}],"title":"NonPositiveDuration","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/nonpositiveduration","role":"symbol"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/ScheduleLabel/onEnter(_:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/schedulelabel\/onenter(_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"onEnter"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16SimulationModule13ScheduleLabelV","text":"ScheduleLabel"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns the label of the schedule that runs when a simulation enters the given state."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/ScheduleLabel\/onEnter(_:)","title":"onEnter(_:)"}}}